      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/man-la-yahduruhu-al-faqih:3:4:4:7",
      "source_url": "https://thaqalayn.net/hadith/34/4/2/3",
      "text": [
        " لاِمْرَأَتِهِ إِنْ تَزَوَّجْتُ عَلَيْكِ أَوْ بِتُّ عَنْكِ فَأَنْتِ طَالِقٌ فَقَالَ \"إِنَّ رَسُولَ اَللَّهِ صَلَّى اَللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَ آلِهِ قَالَ \"مَنْ شَرَطَ شَرْطاً سِوَى كِتَابِ اَللَّهِ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ لَمْ يَجُزْ ذَلِكَ عَلَيْهِ وَ لاَ لَهُ\" \" ، قَالَ وَ سُئِلَ عَنْ رَجُلٍ قَالَ كُلُّ اِمْرَأَةٍ أَتَزَوَّجُهَا مَا عَاشَتْ أُمِّي فَهِيَ طَالِقٌ فَقَالَ \"لاَ طَلاَقَ إِلاَّ بَعْدَ نِكَاحٍ وَ لاَ عِتْقَ إِلاَّ بَعْدَ مِلْكٍ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.4752 - Hammad narrated from Al-Halabi that Abu Abdullah (as) was asked about a man who said to his wife, \"If I marry another woman over you or spend a night away from you, then you are divorced.\"\nImam (as) replied: \"The Messenger of Allah (swt) (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) said: 'Whoever sets a condition outside of the Book of Allah (swt), it is neither binding upon him nor for him.'\"\nImam (as) was also asked about a man who said: \"Any woman I marry while my mother is alive is divorced.\"\nImam (as) replied: \"There is no divorce except after marriage, and no emancipation except after ownership.\""
        ]
      }
    },
